mdgen/mdlint: print uint64_t with PRIx64/PRId64, not %llx/%lld.

Sun built these ILP32, where uint64_t is unsigned long long and %llx is
exact. On an LP64 host uint64_t is unsigned long and every one of the five
sites warns under -Wformat. Same width, same varargs slot, so the output is
identical on every host this project builds on -- this is about a clean
-Wformat, so that the next real format bug is visible instead of the 45th
line of noise. (Sun's own newer files, output_text.c and output_bin.c,
already use <inttypes.h> for exactly this; mdmain.c, output_dot.c and
mdlint.c were never converted.)

All five sites are in the --text and --dot writers. output_bin.c, the only
writer whose bytes QEMU loads, is untouched.

Applied after mdgen-mdlint-host-endian.patch by build/mdtools/gnu/build.sh
to a throwaway copy of src/hypervisor/src/support; src/ is never touched.
Verified 2026-09-22: 1up-md.bin, 1up-hv.bin and both --text outputs
byte-identical before and after (TARGET=pci).

